+## UBU-D0343: General Contractors use bounded coordination mandates and attenuating subdelegation
+
+**Status:** Accepted → DESIGN.md §21.6. Resolves `UBU-Q0081`; refines `UBU-D0138` using `UBU-D0342` and `UBU-D0268` within existing capability, privacy and review boundaries.
+
+Represent the General Contractor role through a versioned CoordinationMandate linking an accountable actor, issuing user or evidenced Association authority, coordination Task/packet, scope, reserved review rights and finite aggregate limits. A role label or prepared packet grants no authority. Association membership claims cannot supply collective authority.
+
+Subdelegation defaults to denied. Each admitted child Task/packet/execution link has one acyclic authority parent and current narrowed grants. Effective authority is the intersection of the complete ancestor chain and current operation policy; privacy, evidence, review and settlement restrictions cannot weaken downstream. Workers retain existing assignment/lease/retry semantics; human and Association work requires accepted scoped commitments.
+
+Account for contractor overhead, descendants, retries and nested coordination against shared root/branch ceilings using atomic reservations and cumulative counters. Reports retain source attribution and remain candidate evidence. Originators retain policy-permitted inspection, pause, revocation and final review; delivery or contractor summaries cannot establish Task/Objective success or authorize settlement.
+
+Invalidation applies transitively at dispatch, privileged action, disclosure, result release and admission, with explicit assignment cancellation and honest handling of late output and irreversible effects. DESIGN.md §21.6 specifies schema, lifecycle, propagation and enablement fixtures. Phase 1 remains unchanged; this decision accepts a post-MVP data-model contract, not shipped contractor coordination, Association governance or marketplace/settlement protocols.
